---
import '../../styles/global.css'
import '@orbex/sonar-components/styles.css'
import Demo from '../../components/Demo.astro'
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro'
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro'
import Confirm from '../../demos/dialog/Confirm.tsx'
import confirmCode from '../../demos/dialog/Confirm.tsx?raw'
import Tones from '../../demos/notice/Tones.tsx'
import tonesCode from '../../demos/notice/Tones.tsx?raw'
import Undo from '../../demos/toast/Undo.tsx'
import undoCode from '../../demos/toast/Undo.tsx?raw'
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'
import DoDont from '../../components/DoDont.astro'
import SpecimenFigure from '../../components/SpecimenFigure.astro'
import '@orbex/sonar-patterns/app/app-tokens.css'
import '@orbex/sonar-patterns/app/assistant.css'

const choices = [
  ['Something just happened', 'Toast', 'Layout saved. Order PO-2210 created.'],
  ['It can be taken back', 'Toast with Undo', 'Inventory removed from your overview.'],
  ['It cannot be taken back', 'Dialog, before acting', 'Reset the overview? Discard the new order?'],
  ['A state that lasts', 'Notice, in place', '2 invoices overdue. The carrier changed.'],
  ['A field is wrong', 'Error under the field', 'Choose a date from May 12 on.'],
]
---

<Docs title="Feedback" description="How Sonar-DB tells people what happened: toasts, undo, confirmations, notices and field errors, and when to use each.">
  <PageHeader
    title="Feedback"
    lead="Say what happened, close to where it happened, and only interrupt for what cannot be undone. Most actions act at once and offer an Undo; a confirmation is the exception."
  />

  <Section title="Which one" id="which">
    <div class="table-wrap" data-scroll-region data-label="Which feedback to use">
      <table>
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Which feedback to use</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">When</th>
            <th scope="col">Use</th>
            <th scope="col">Example</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {choices.map(([when, use, example]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{when}</th>
              <td>{use}</td>
              <td>{example}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Act, then offer to undo" id="undo">
    <Demo title="Saved, and removed with undo" code={undoCode}><Undo client:visible /></Demo>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Confirm what cannot be undone" id="confirm">
    <Demo title="Resetting the overview" code={confirmCode}><Confirm client:visible /></Demo>
  </Section>

  <Section title="States that last" id="notices">
    <Demo title="Notices" code={tonesCode} layout="list"><Tones /></Demo>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Loading" id="loading">
    <p class="prose">
      The product waits in two places, and each shows it in place, with the words of what is happening rather than an empty
      shape. While the search reads a query, its status line says “Understanding “…”…” and a light band in the accent
      green crosses the words once a second; the results replace it. While the AI assistant writes an answer, three dots
      pulse in its bubble, 1 s each, 150 ms apart. Cards arrive with their data, so the overview has no skeleton screens; a
      module that someday needs to load reuses the shimmer on its own words. With reduced motion requested, the words
      stay still and the dots stop.
    </p>
    <SpecimenFigure title="Search, reading the query">
      <div class="sonar-search-status loading-specimen"><span class="sonar-shimmer">Understanding “delayed deliveries this week”…</span></div>
    </SpecimenFigure>
    <SpecimenFigure title="AI assistant, writing an answer">
      <div class="oxa loading-specimen"><div class="cw-m them"><div class="cw-bub typing" role="img" aria-label="The assistant is thinking"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div></div>
    </SpecimenFigure>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Writing it" id="writing">
    <ul class="prose">
      <li>Past tense for what happened (“Layout saved.”), a question for a decision (“Reset the overview?”).</li>
      <li>Name the thing: “Inventory removed”, not “Item removed”.</li>
      <li>The button that answers a question repeats its verb: Reset, Discard. Never Yes or OK.</li>
      <li>No exclamation marks and no apologies. Errors say how to fix them.</li>
    </ul>
  </Section>
  <DoDont page="feedback" />
</Docs>

<style>
  .table-wrap {
    /* One axis only: wide content scrolls sideways; nothing scrolls or bounces up and down */
    overflow: auto hidden;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    border-radius: var(--sonar-shape-corner-medium);
    background: var(--sonar-color-surface-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sonar-elevation-1);
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 560px;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font: var(--sonar-type-body-md);
  }

  th,
  td {
    padding: var(--sonar-space-12) var(--sonar-space-16);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sonar-color-divider);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  thead th {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-tertiary);
    font: var(--sonar-type-label-md);
  }

  tbody th {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-strong);
    font-weight: var(--sonar-font-weight-medium);
  }

  td:nth-child(2) {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-strong);
  }

  td:last-child {
    color: var(--sonar-color-text-secondary);
  }
</style>
